ted  2 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of fibroadipose tissue  2 frags  ESS   CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_CASE_ID   awe ag  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by William R Welch M D   Electronically signed on Monday  REMOVED_MONTH 15   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 23 27PM  SURGICAL ADDENDUM   A prior core needle biopsy for a 0 5cm mass revealed a 0 25cm invasive  carcinoma that was ER and PR positive and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu negative   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    No  residual invasive carcinoma was seen in this specimen after complete  microscopic evaluation of the margin  However  the gel pledgets marking the  center of the core needle biopsy site are present at the junction of the deep  and medial margins and the breast tissue at this aspect of the biopsy cannot be  evaluated  Clinical correlation is necessary to determine if there is breast  tissue present at this location or if this margin is at the pectoral muscle   The appropriate AJCC classification  6th edition  is  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   sn    Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for DCIS  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor POSITIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NEGATIVE  1    Immunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following  criteria   Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the  carcinoma is reported as follows   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low   0      10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  of nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clini