located in the  upper outer quadrant  The first biopsy site  0 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm   is located in  the upper outer quadrant deep to the skin ellipse  The second biopsy site of  hemorrhage measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm is located inferior and posterior to  the first biopsy cavity and is closer to the resection margin  0 2cm from  deep resection margin   The closest of the two  2  biopsy cavities approach  one another is 0 9cm  In addition  careful sectioning reveals in the lower  inner quadrant additional area of hemorrhage  which may or may not represent  biopsy site measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  This site is located 4 5cm from  the other site s  of biopsy  Careful sectioning of the axillary tissue  reveals the presence of fourteen  14  candidate lymph nodes which are entirely  submitted for analysis   Micro 1  1st biopsy site in relation closest to skin surface  2 frags  RSS   Micro 2  1st biopsy site in relation to deep margin perpendicular  2 frags   RSS   Micro 3  1st biopsy site  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  2nd biopsy cavity  closer to deep margin   and lower outer  quadrant  perpendicular  2 frags per cass   RSS   Micro 6  biopsy site versus hemorrhage located in lower inner quadrant   2 frags  RSS   Micro 7  deep margin perpendicular  lower inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS   Micro 8  deep margin perpendicular  upper inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS   Micro 9  upper outer quadrant  deep margin perpendicular  2 frags  RSS   Micro 10  skin with cicatrix  2 frags  RSS   Micro 11  skin with nipple  1 frag  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  4 candidate lymph nodes per cass   4 frags per cass   ESS   Micro 15  2 candidate lymph nodes  2 frags  ESS   Part two  labeled   2  additional axillary node   and consists of a single  fragment of tan white soft tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The entire  specimen is submitted for histologic analysis   Micro 16  additional axillary node  1 frag  ESS   Reports to  CARTER  KATH