ures REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The  specimen is serially sectioned and reveals an irregular white fibrotic lesion  that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 1cm  In one of the slices this lesion is adjacent  to the black inked posterior margin corresponding to the area of retraction   The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable and is composed of  approximately 90  yellow adipose tissue with 10  being interlacing white  fibrous bands   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   white fibrous mass lesion adjacent to posterior margin  1  frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   additional representations of the mass  1 frag each  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   upper outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lower outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lower inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   upper inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   nipple  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   skin scar  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   additional representation of white fibrous mass with  respect  to deep margin  1 frag  RSS   Part B  labeled   2   right breast skin   consists of two fragments of skin   3 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm    There are no visible scars or  lesions present on the skin   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections of right breast skin  2 frags  RSS   ROH lp  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Resident Review by Michael H Roh M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Final Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  9 16  REMOVED_CASE_ID    report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
