ly hemorrhagic soft  tissues  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate   which are submitted in toto   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contents of white cassettes with green lids  multi frags in each   ESS   Part B  labeled  left breast site  2   contains four white cassettes with blue  lids with multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues  3 0  x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate   which are submitted in toto   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contents of white cassettes with blue lid  multi frags in each   ESS   CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    JC ag  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Friday  February 13   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 17 27PM  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  2 19 09    Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for invasive carcinoma  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NEGATIVE  1    Note  Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for  progesterone receptors   Immunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following  criteria   Hormone receptor analysis   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low   0      10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  of nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not  yet been determined    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu analysis   Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but  only a portion of the membrane is positive   Equivocal  2   Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells   Positive  3   Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells   Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   External controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity   Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational  use only   Addendum  1 by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on Thursday  February 19   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07 44 28PM  SURGICAL ADDENDUM   An immunoperoxidase study for e cadherin is performed on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although  the invasive carcinoma has lobular morphology  the carcinoma is moderately  immunoreactive  Therefore  this is an unusual lobular carcinoma with  e cadherin expression  Some of the in situ carcinoma is also e cadherin  positive  Other cells have weak or absent expression  Final classification of  both components should be made on the excisional specimen   Addendum  2 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Wednesday  REMOVED_MONTH 22   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07 24 18PM   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
