ularity but there  are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma  The specimen is  entirely submitted   MICRO  1 7  Central area of specimen  where two localizing wires were located    mult frags  ESS   MICRO  8 10  Portion of specimen lateral to central region of breast  mult  frags  ESS   MICRO  11 13  Portion of specimen medial to central region of breast  mult  frags  ESS   Reports to  CHRISTIAN  ROGER  L  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 54 CLINICAL DATA  History of right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Grade  3 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  Location of the ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the mass  Margin of the ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the posterior margin of the specimen focally  Stains for receptors  Requested  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN INFERIOR    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL NODE    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE EXAMINED LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunostains are negative for keratin positive tumor cells  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 19 22                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  right breast excision  is a lumpectomy specimen measuring 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm with a needle localization wire  The entire specimen is inked black  posterior margin overinked blue  superior margin overinked yellow and inferior margin overinked orange  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm gritty white nodule present 0 2cm from the deep resection margin and 0 5cm from the inferior resection margin  Representative sections of the nodule and closest proximity to the resection margin is submitted in cassettes A C  Grossly normal breast parenchyma away from nodule in cassette D  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  sentinel lymph node  is one 1 7cm lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette E  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  additional deep margin inferior  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in aggregate  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes F H  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  final shave margin  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm in aggregate  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes I M  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Bradford Marshall Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION