tions  Extremely minute focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on low grade micropapillary ductal carcinoma in situ  see note  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT TOCC REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD MIHN DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  In specimen B  in the breast tissue adjacent to the fibroadenoma  there is a very small focus of atypical cells that is at least atypical ductal hyperplasia  This focus resembles the ductal carcinoma in situ seen in specimen A  However  given the very small size of this focus  a definitive diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ cannot be made  An immunohistochemical stain for estrogen receptors will be performed on specimen A and the results will be reported in an addendum to follow  Final Diagnosis by  Nicole A  Mihok  M D  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT TOCC REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT TOCC REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD MIHN Notes  REMOVED_DATE In addition to the co signer  Drs  Misialek  Ross  Feen and Mattia have seen the case and concur with the above written diagnoses  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT TOCC ADDENDUM REPORTAddendum  1 Entered  10 29 08  REMOVED_CASE_ID      ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION     This report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information  The original diagnosis is unchanged  Immunohistochemical staining on the formalin fixed  paraffin embedded block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reveals these results for the ductal carcinoma in situ  Estrogen receptor  POSITIVE   10  of nuclei stained  Estrogen receptor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and or progesterone receptor  PgR 1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   is assessed visually by quantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining Addendum Final  MIHOK NICOLE MD        REMOVED_DATE  10 29 08  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD MIHN Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORDCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Obstruction  NO  REMOVE