Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D   RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS   SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN  SITU  is present in three of 13 blocks  2  4  and 6  levels examined    Extensive ADH lining mucin filled cysts is present in ten of thirteen   10 13  blocks   ADH is present   0 1cm from multiple inked margins  not oriented    Note  Multiple small foci  each   0 2cm   of ADH closely approach a  diagnosis of DCIS  However  given the small size of each focus  a  diagnosis of ADH is favored  Excision is recommended due to the  difficulty in distinguishing ADH from small foci of DCIS in this specimen  and the histologic similarity between the areas approaching a diagnosis of  DCIS and the ADH   There are areas of extravesated mucin in stroma associated with  mucin filled cysts  Additional levels do not reveal epithelial cells  within the mucin  Therefore  no invasive carcinoma is seen   This case was reviewed at the Staff Pathology Conference   CLINICAL DATA   History  Microcalcifications in right breast   TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Tissue from right breast   Mammography  Calcifications are in the specimen      Dr  Darrell Smith  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by BUNDOCK ELIZABETH A  M D  PH D   The specimen is received fresh in one part  labeled with the patient s name and  unit number  and consists of one  1  unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue   4 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm   with areas of firm tan white fibrotic tissue   approximately one third of the specimen   The localization wire is received  unattached to mass and free floating in specimen container  The specimen is  received with mammogram  demonstrating calcifications in the specimen   The specimen is sectioned to reveal poorly defined areas of fibrosis with one   1  area  1 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm    which may contain calcifications based on  palpation  The specimen is submitted entirely as follows   Micro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue containing possible calcifications  mult frags  ESS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of breast tissue  17 frags  ESS   eab  Reports to  CHRISTIAN  ROGER  L  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
