Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  Report Status  Signed  Type  Surgical Pathology  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS   Left breast  excision   Atypical ductal hyperplasia  severe  with microcalcifications   NOTE  The previous left breast needle biopsies are reviewed  S 01  REMOVED_CASE_ID    The  excision biopsy demonstrates severely atypical ductal hyperplasia which  in some foci have a histomorphology suggestive of ductal carcinoma in  situ  This case has been consulted with two breast pathologists  Dr   Frederick Koerner from Massachusetts General Hospital  who finds there  is sufficient change for a diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ and Dr   Stuart Schnitt from Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center  who feels the  changes represent severely atypical ductal hyperplasia borderline ductal  carcinoma in situ  See both consultation reports sent to you under  separate cover  The changes  in my opinion  reside on the borderline of  severely atypical ductal hyperplasia ductal carcinoma in situ spectrum   The atypical ductal hyperplasia ductal carcinoma in situ changes are  present at the inked surgical margins   Final Diagnosis by  Dennis J  Feen  M D   Clinical diagnosis   history   Left breast mass  Tissue Designation   Breast  excision with margins   left  Gross description   The specimen labeled  breast mass  is received in formalin and consists of an  oval mass of yellowish  fibrocollagenous tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  A short  suture designates the superior margin and a long suture designates the lateral  margin  The superior margin and the lateral margin are inked with blue ink   The cut surface reveals a recent area of hemorrhage at one edge and some  greyish white fibrous tissue in the area of the hemorrhage  No discrete masses  or cysts are noted  11X all   Dictated by  DJF____ signature on file ____MICHAEL J  ROSS  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final   ____ signature on file ____RICHARD SAMPSON  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final   ____ signature on file ____DENNIS J  FEEN  M D  REMOVED_DATE  Final    report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
