Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 3 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Atypia in prior core biopsy specimen  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH RARE SMALL CALCIFICATIONS AND USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY OR ATYPIA  NOTE  The previously obtained core biopsy specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   is reviewed and its interpretation confirmed  The atypical focus in that specimen  which is a generous sample of tissue  is well demarcated by dense coarse calcifications  No residual atypical epithelium is identified in the current excision specimen  The healing biopsy site is submitted entirely for microscopical examination  The resection margins of the current specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh  labeled Christin Schulze   252 60 62 and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm irregular portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior  a long stitch designating lateral  and a needle localization wire in place  The specimen is received with a specimen radiograph  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  inferior   yellow  The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with a prior biopsy site  The cavity extends to within 0 1cm of the anterior  2 0cm of the posterior  1 1cm of the superior  and 2 5cm of the inferior margin  The cavity is greater than 2cm from both the medial and lateral ends  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a moderate amount of interspersed nodular grey white fibrous tissue  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  No clip is identified on cut section  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the body of specimen  to include the cavity  sequentially from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end  en face  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 10   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 00 53PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left   Excision  report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
