Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  KATHARINE CARTER M D   CASE  BS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Resident  Eric C Huang  M D   Ph D   Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST  3 00  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A 10 CM AREA OF MRI ENHANCEMENT  ASSOCIATED WITH A PALPABLE SUBAREOLAR MASS   EXTENSIVE ATYPICAL HYPERPLASIA associated with numerous intraductal papillomas  with florid epithelial hyperplasia  present throughout the specimen  completely  examined microscopically in 38 blocks  see note    Focal mucin production is associated with areas of ADH  e g  block 18  levels  examined    ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA with signet ring cells is best seen in the  original level of block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   This area is no longer present on deeper levels  used for immunohistochemical studies  Adjacent areas of ADH are immunoreactive  for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and e cadherin  and are negative  for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu   Myoepithelial cells are present in papillary areas  immunohistochemical study  for p63  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The palpable mass corresponds to an area of intraductal papillomas   Note  This is a difficult to classify hyperplasia due to the extensive  involvement of papillomas  the florid hyperplasia  and the presence of lobular  neoplasia  In focal areas  micropapillae are formed  e g   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     However  these areas are insufficient for a diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in  situ   The entire specimen is examined microscopically  including margins   This case was also reviewed by Dr  Deborah Dillon  who concurs with this  interpretation   CLINICAL DATA   History  History of left nipple discharge with 1 5cm mass at edge of areola at  3 o clock and abnormal left MRI with abnormal enhancement posterior to nipple   Operation  Left breast biopsy with MRI guided biopsy   Operative Findings  Not provided   Clinical Diagnosis  Left nipple discharge   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A  Left breast tissue at 3 o clock  2 stitches close together   marks  subareolar mass  please comment on what this is  short   superior  long    lateral  RADIOLOGY   MRI loc   please process all tissue   Density and   distortion are in specimen at wire  There is also a palpable  finding in the specimen   possible mammographic correlate is marked   2    Dr  E P  Frost  GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patients name and unit number  and consists of a lumpectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE  medial to lateral  x REMOVED_DATE  superior  to inferior  x REMOVED_DATE  anterior to posterior cm with a localization wire  There  is a long suture designated as lateral and a short suture designated as  superior and a double stitch designated as  subareolar mass  per surgeon   The specimen radiograph shows an ill defined area of tissue density traversed  by the wire  which has been annotated as  1 by the radiologist  This area is  in the lateral portion of the specimen  At the medial end of the specimen   another ill defined density has been circled and annotated by the radiologist  as   2    palpable lesion    The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins   posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow   medial orange  The palpable area corresponding to the sutures marking the  subareolar mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and abuts the medial margin  and is  0 3cm from the posterior margin  1 1cm from the inferior margin  1 1cm from  the superior margin  1 5cm from the anterior margin  and   2 0cm from the  lateral margin  The subareolar mass consists of multiple small granular  palpable foci without a discrete mass   The ill defined tissue density in the lateral portion of the specimen measures  2 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  This area is present at the lateral margin  0 6cm from  the anterior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin  1 2cm from the superior  margin    2 0cm from the inferior and medial margins  The specimen consists  of 85  adipose tissue and 15  of fibrous firm tissue  The entire specimen is  submitted  The gross specimen is reviewed with Dr  Susan Lester of the Breast  Pathology Service   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   palpable subareolar mass  medial margin  3 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   palpable subareolar mass  anterior  posterior  superior  and  inferior margins  5 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   tissue between the two densities in the midportion of the  specimen  anterior  posterior  superior  and inferior margins  4 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral mass per radiograph  lateral  anterior  posterior   superior  and inferior margins  8 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   remainder of the specimen  18 frags  ESS   ECH ajb  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  5 23  REMOVED_CASE_ID    report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST COMPREHENSIVE  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D   CONSULT SLIDES RECEIVED FROM MORTON HOSPITAL  TAUNTON  MA   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  96  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 26 96    Apocrine cysts   NOTE  According to the original report  the specimen radiograph did not  show any abnormalities   CONSULT SLIDES RECEIVED FROM STURDY MEMORIAL HOSPITAL  ATTLEBORO  MA   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   6 12 96    Multifocal lactational changes  blocks A to C  see NOTE    Atypical lobular hyperplasia  block D    Apocrine metaplasia   Numerous benign calcifications   A prior biopsy site is present   NOTE  The areas of lactational changes are somewhat unusual in that in  some areas the lactational changes involve areas of epithelial  hyperplasia  Of note  the changes are restricted to the lobular units and  do not involve the terminal ducts   The cytologic and architectural features are felt to be insufficient for a  diagnosis of DCIS   Lactational changes can be seen in response to pregnancy or hormone use  but are also seen as an incidental finding   This case was also reviewed at the BWH staff conference   RIGHT BREAST  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   9 13 99    Apocrine adenosis with numerous calcifications   Epithelial hyperplasia   LEFT BREAST  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   9 27 99    Lobules with calcifications   Apocrine cysts   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 47 year old female with history of multiple bilateral breast  biopsies  left breast biopsy on REMOVED_DATE at BWH  benign   right breast wire  localized biopsy on REMOVED_DATE  Morton Hospital  for inner lower quadrant  calcifications showing fibrocystic changes  right breast excision for  calcifications on REMOVED_DATE  Sturdy Memorial Hospital  with