  posterior  Two wires are present in the specimen  The more lateral of the two  is arbitrarily designated wire  1  This wire enters laterally  0 4cm from the  anterior margin and 1 9cm from the superior and inferior margins  It exits  laterally  0 8cm from the superior margin and 1 5cm from the posterior  margin  A radiograph shows this wire passing through one ill defined mass and  adjacent to mammography clip  Wire  2 enters anteriorly  1 0cm from the  lateral margin and 0 7cm from the inferior margin  It exits at the junction  of the anterior and superior margins  0 5cm from the lateral margin  A  radiograph shows this wire passing adjacent to a mammography clip  There is no  clear mass specimen in this area  The entire specimen is serially sectioned  from medial to lateral into eleven slices  such that slice  1 represents the  medial margin and slice  11 represents the lateral margin  The specimen  consists of approximately 70  firm  pink white  fibrous tissue and 30  yellow  adipose tissue  Both mammography clips are identified and removed  Please  note  While the clinical history describes two separate lesions  these grossly  appear to be contiguous  The two clips are 1 0cm apart  No discrete mass is  identified  The entire specimen is submitted   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  perpendicular sections  11 frags total  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  2  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  3  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  4  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  5  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  6  1 frag per cassette  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  7  1 frag per cassette  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  8  1 frag per cassette  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  9 including clip site  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  9  tissue adjacent to clip site  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  9  tissue between clip