 REMOVED_CASE_ID  SHILAS DALIA 41 F  REG REF 05 07    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC GRABOWSKY TARA A  M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  05 07 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  Baseline mammogram showed multiple clusters of indeterminate calcifications of right retroareolar lower central and upper outer quadrant    fibrocystic changes vs ductal carcinoma in situ Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereo biopsies  right breast calcifications  and consists of two aqua cassettes  which are designated on the specimen requisition as the right retroareolar lower central breast with calcifications  The first cassette contains three firm  yellowish red needle biopsies ranging in size from 1 6cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter to 2 2cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter  3X all  labeled 1  The second aqua cassette contains a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  aggregate of reddish tan  firm  glistening needle biopsies  each measuring 0 3cm  in diameter  1 agg  all  labeled 2  Also present in the same container is a 2 x 1 x 0 3cm  aggregate of reddish tan  firm needle biopsies with attached blood clot  each measuring 0 3cm  in diameter  1 agg  all  labeled 3  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DIAGNOSIS  Right breast  lower central retroareolar  needle biopsy  Calcifications associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  This case was reviewed by Dr  Frederick Koerner  Massachusetts General Hospital  who rendered the following opinion   I find this case especially challenging and I cannot give you a precise diagnosis  The calcifications of concern distort several ducts and ductules  and the associated ductal cells look atypical  They appear enlarged and they possess large and somewhat pleomorphic nuclei and homogeneous chromatin  A few nuclei contain conspicuous nucleoli  I would not interpret these areas as foci of ductal hyperplasia  the nuclei appear too big  and the presence of calcifications would not fit with that interpretation  The cells could represent a carcinoma  however  the foci do not exhibit an obvious increase in the number of epithelial cells  In the absence of cellular proliferation and marked anaplasia  I cannot recognize the cells as malignant  Degenerative changes can sometimes cause nuclear enlargement and pleomorphism  and such a phenomenon might explain the appearance of these cells  These degenerative effects usually cause the chromatin to become dark and smudgy rather than pale  as seen in the case at hand  so I do not feel comfortable with this interpretation  DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT   Continued  either  I would therefore make the diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia and suggest that the patient undergo an excision of this region of the right breast  After examining the adjacent tissue  I expect that you will be able to reach a secure diagnosis   Final Diagnosis by  Jean L  Fraser  M D  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD FRAJE Notes  REMOVED_DATE  All nine slides ret d  jam  CR  REMOVED_DATE  Path report faxed  jam REMOVED_DATE  Dr  Koerner s report rec d  djd REMOVED_DATE  Sent all nine slides to Dr  Frederick Koerner   MGH via courier for opinion JLF jam  CO   617  REMOVED_DATE Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Right breast  N BREANBX    BREANBX BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Atypical hyperp Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCOPIES TO  GRABOWSKY TARA A  M D  P O  Box 469 MEDFIELD  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   508 359  REMOVED_CASE_ID  SELLAND DONNA LEE M D  NEWTON WELLESLEY RADIOLOGY NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 243  REMOVED_CASE_ID MARKERS  Breast Disease Related  Consult Case Out  Consult Case Return Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJPROCEDURES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   05 11 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJTISSUES  Breast  needle biopsy   right  retroareolar  lower central Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJFinal  ROSS MICHAEL J  M D    REMOVED_DATE  05 11 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD ROSMJ FRASER JEAN L  MD      REMOVED_DATE  05 11 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD FRAJE                                                                                              , no_TubularCancer.
