Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 AUG 01 ACCESSIONED ON  08 AUG 01 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA  Two areas of calcification left breast  DCIS on core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF EXTENSIVE SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 2 of 15 blocks  Spanning at least 0 8cm  Grade  1 Calcifications  In the carcinoma in situ  atypical ductal hyperplasia and in benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 1cm from the lateral margin of the specimen in one focus  NOTE  Atypical ductal hyperplasia is focally present at the deep margin  and is  0 1cm from the deep and lateral margins in several foci  The ductal carcinoma in situ is found in the more central portion of the specimen closer to the clip  whereas the second area of calcification represents severely atypical ductal hyperplasia  BREAST  LEFT   SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT   INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  15 AUG 01 at 15 37                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  and  left breast wide excision  is a 6 x 4 x 3cm portion of breast tissue with two needle localization wires attached  The specimen is oriented with the short stitch denotating the superior margin and a long stitch denoting the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  media