Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  KRANE  JEFFREY  FRED  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by KRANE JEFFREY FRED M D  PH D   LEFT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZATION OF A PRIOR CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY SITE   Focal epithelial hyperplasia   There is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen   including margins   Note  The patient had a prior core needle biopsy for calcifications which  revealed atypical ductal hyperplasia  A clip was not placed   The original calcifications were removed by the core needle biopsy  The  radiologist localized an area consistent with a hematoma for this  excision  In the specimen radiograph  the radiologist noted two benign  appearing calcifications  not definitively associated with the biopsy  site   The specimen radiograph reveals very faint possible calcifications and a  small density  The entire specimen is submitted for histologic  examination  and multiple levels are examined  including margins  No  definite calcifications are identified  The blocks are radiographed and a  possible small calcification is located in block 3  Multiple levels do  not reveal histologic evidence of calcification   A biopsy site or hematoma consistent with the prior core needle biopsy  site are not identified  Clinical and radiologic correlation is suggested  to ensure that this excision includes the site of the prior core needle  biopsy   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 65 year old postmenopausal female  on hormone replacement therapy  whose recent mammogram demonstrated a 5mm cluster of calcifications  in the left breast  Core biopsy revealed atypical ductal hyperplasia   Operation  Left breast wire localization excision  Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast ADH  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Left breast mass  RADIOLOGY  Two benign appearing calcifications in specimen  not definitely  associated with the biopsy site  J  Leung  MD  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by OH KIRSTINE YUNG TING M D   The specimen is received fresh in one part  labeled with the patient s name   unit number and  left breast mass inking per pathology protocol   Attached  with the specimen is a mammogram demonstrating a fragment of breast tissue with  a wire localizing needle in the specimen  a small density  and very faint  calcifications  The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm and is received inked  per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black   anterior   blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial    orange  Serial sectioning reveals yellow tan fatty tissue throughout the  specimen  No focal lesions or fibrous tissue is identified  The specimen is  entirely submitted from medial to lateral   Micro 1  medial border of breast tissue  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections of breast tissue  1 frag each  ESS  Micro 11  lateral border of breast tissue  2 frags  ESS  ko  Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
