argin  in twelve  slices  Sectioning reveals the breast parenchyma to be composed of greater  than 95  dense white fibrous tissue with less than 5  fatty tissue  The wire  ends in slice four  There are no grossly apparent masses or calcifications   The specimen is radiographed  showing calcifications in slice four and possible  calcifications in slices one  two and eight  The entire specimen is submitted   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice one  superior margin  en face   1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice two  superior and anterior margins   2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice three  superior  inferior  posterior margins   2  frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice four  inferior  superior  medial margins   2 frags   ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice five  inferior  medial  superior margins   3 frags   ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice six  inferior  medial  superior margins   4 frags   ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice seven  inferior  superior  medial margins   2 frags   ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice eight  inferior  superior  medial margins   4 frags   ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice nine  superior  medial  lateral margins   2 frags   ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice ten  medial  inferior  deep  lateral margins   2  frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice eleven  medial  lateral  inferior  deep margins   2  frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   slice twelve  lateral and deep margins  en face   1 frag   ESS   JUB lp  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Resident Review by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  10 11  REMOVED_CASE_ID    report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
