ve carcinoma is present on 3 of 16 slides as a 0 8cm focus on each  slide  close to lateral margin  the involved slides likely represent the same  focus of invasive carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The carcinoma in situ shows a  spectrum of morphology ranging from classic low nuclear grade LCIS to CIS of  intermediate grade with solid and cribriform cohesive architecture   Intermediate grade CIS has various patterns  discohesive with single cell  necrosis  CIS with micropapillary and cribriform features   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and CIS  involving intraductal papillomas which due to papillary architecture present  makes it difficult to distinguish LCIS from DCIS  CIS is associated with  calcifications but it is likely some of the calcifications in neoplastic ducts  were preexisting in the breast epithelium  For the purpose of margin  evaluation  margins have been reported for all but the classic low nuclear  grade LCIS present   CLINICAL DATA   History  Abnormal mammo  LT breast  Operation  Wire directed excision  abnormal LT breast  Operative Findings  Abnormal area LT breast  Clinical Diagnosis  See op note  TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left breast tissue  long suture lateral  short suture superior  GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  long suture lateral  short suture superior   consists  of an irregular pink tan to tan yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast  tissue  4 0cm anterior to posterior  3 0cm superior to inferior  and 2 6cm  medial to lateral  with a short suture designating the superior margin  and a  long suture designating the lateral margins  There is a needle localization  wire which enters through the anterior superior aspect of the specimen and  exits through the posterior lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is  inked per pathology protocol  superior red  inferior green  medial orange   lateral yellow