Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D   LEFT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS   SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  involving adenosis within a  hyalinized fibroadenoma in two of 10 slides  slides 3 and 4  levels  examined   see note    Calcifications are associated with the ADH and with the fibroadenoma   Apocrine cysts   Note  There is an area of adenosis within the fibroadenoma which is  expanded by a population of monomorphic cells with low grade nuclei   Occasional small cribriform spaces are formed  There is also pagetoid  spread into the larger ducts  This cellular proliferation is limited  to the fibroadenoma  and is not seen outside the area of the fibroadenoma   Although this proliferation may represent a small area of low grade DCIS   a diagnosis of severely atypical ductal hyperplasia is prefered due  to the limited nature of the process  Dr  Andrea Richardson reviewed  selected slides and concurs   The ADH is   0 1cm from the inferior and medial margins  Re excision may  be helpful due to the possibility of DCIS   Some of the calcifiations appear to be associated with the ADH  However   the majority of the calcifications appear to be associated with the  fibroadenoma   CLINICAL DATA   History  Abnormal mammogram   Operation  Left needle directed breast bx   Clinical Diagnosis  Abnormal mammogram   TISSUE SUBMITTED  Tissue from left breast   RADIOLOGY  Ca   in specimen  OR called  Dr  E  Frost  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by PADERA ROBERT F  JR  M D  PH D   The specimen is received in formalin in one part  labeled with the patient s  name and medical record number and the description   1 tissue from left  breast   The specimen consists of a fragment of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The specimen is received with two orienting  sutures  The double long suture is present at the lateral margin and the  double short suture is present at the posterior margin  The specimen is  received six inked according to pathology protocol for the evaluation  of margins  posterior   black  anterior   blue  superior   red  inferior    green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange  The specimen is received with a wire  in place  The radiograph is examined and reveals the area of calcifications is  present in the inferior half of the specimen in the lateral aspect  The  localization wire is present within this area   The tissue at the area of the calcifications is composed primarily of adipose  tissue with thick intervening fibrous bands and nodules  This area corresponds  to a fibrous area that is primarily submitted in blocks REMOVED_DATE The specimen is  serially sectioned  The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic  examination   Micro REMOVED_DATE  region of calcifications  5 frags  ESS   Micro 6  representative sections of superior margin  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen  mult frags  ESS   rp  Reports to  CHRISTIAN  ROGER  L  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
