d fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number   and  left breast   and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm excision of  fibroadipose tissue  oriented by sutures designating superior  short suture    lateral  long suture   and deep margin  whipstitch   The specimen is inked per  pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black   anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange   inked by surgeon   The localizing wire enters the specimen inferomedially and  exits posteriorly  The accompanying radiograph shows a localizing wire in  place within the specimen adjacent to an encircled area of an ill defined dense  mass  Sectioning demonstrates tan white focally granular fibrous tissue  at  least 40  of the specimen   with an area of hemorrhage associated with the  localizing wire tract  Fibrous tissue in the area of interest shows focal  dilated ducts filled with a tan yellow  thick fluid  at least 2 5cm in  greatest dimension  abutting multiple margins  particularly inferior and  posterior  Associated fibrous tissue radiates to all margins  There are no  definitive masses  Entire specimen is submitted  sequentially from inferior to  superior  with area of interest as marked by wire in micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire specimen  multiple frags  ESS  Note  Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     inferior  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    inferior  lateral  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     lateral  medial  inferior  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    posterior  lateral   medial  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    inferior  medial  lateral  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     posterior  medial  lateral  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    anterior  lateral   micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    posterior  medial  lateral  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    lateral   anterior  medial  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    medial  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    posterior   lateral  medial  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    medial  posterior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     posterior  lateral  superior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    superior  medial  micro   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    superior  medial  posterior  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    medial   superior  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    medial  superior  posterior  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     medial  micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    superior  Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are  inferior and superior margins  perpendicular sections   respectively    db lp  CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_CASE_ID    By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  10 6  REMOVED_CASE_ID    report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
