Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA  Biopsy showed lobular carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  BIOPSY SITE WITH ACUTE AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HEMOSIDERIN LADEN MACROPHAGES  AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CYSTS AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  4  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  5  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Seven of seven lymph nodes are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 56                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast and axillary tail which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  The overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 6cm  5 0cm lateral to the nipple is a curved healed scar  The nipple and areolar are grossly unremarkable  Corresponding to the healed scar area beneath this is a previous biopsy cavity which is small and surrounded by hard firm yellow tissue  Adjacent to this more medially is a stellate firm  hard mass which is approximately 0 2cm from an inked surface  More medially are other areas which are firm  stellate  white and irregular  Sections around the biopsy site are in A through D  more medially there are several areas of firm  white hard parenchyma  One such stellate area is most medial and is approximately 0 4cm from an inked margin  and is submitted in E  Another region very close to the anterior inked margin is submitted in F  Lateral and inferior to the biopsy cavity is a firm  white irregular area abutting an inked margin  which is submitted in G  Towards the axillary tail and inferior is an irregular stellate area approximating an inked margin as submitted in H  Examination of the axillary tail reveals seven possible lymph nodes ranging in dimension from 0 4cm to 2 0cm  These lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes I through M  Additional sections of breast parenchyma are submitted in N through Q  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Allan Enrique Pineda  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
