Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Signed Out by  Kristina Braaten  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Tissue Processed CLINICAL DATA  None provided  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  NODULAR PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA ASSOCIATED WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SMALL FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   SEE NOTE   FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Results of an immunohistochemical stain for E cadherin appear to support the suspicion of atypical lobular hyperplasia  however  because there are only a few cells and they are not optimally preserved  the findings fall short of a definitive diagnosis  Additional tissue sections will be submitted for evaluation and an addendum will follow  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled Ana Pires   448 35 85  and  right breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow pink fibrofatty soft tissue with a needle localization wire in place  There is a long suture designating the lateral a short designating anterior and a bowtie designating the cephalad aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a well circumscribed  lobulated tan white rubbery mass containing a metal clip and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The mass abuts the posterior inferior margin  comes to 0 4cm from the superior  0 6cm from the anterior  0 4cm from the lateral and 3 0cm from the medial margins  respectively  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow lobulated and grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin taken radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass to closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin taken en face  Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  Microscopic examination of additional tissue sections   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   is non contributory  Results of an immunohistochemical stain for keratin REMOVED_DATE support the diagnoses of usual ductal hyperplasia and focal atypical ductal hyperplasia as reported above  Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
