Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Skin biopsy  other than cyst  tag  debrid or repair  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  HARLEY A HAYNES M D   CASE  BS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  MOYA  Resident  Marianna B Ruzinova  M D   Ph D   Pathologist  Scott R Granter  M D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A  SKIN  LEFT SCALP  PUNCH     Dermal mucin deposition and pigment incontinence     Mostly anagen and one catagen follicle are seen     Multiple levels examined   NOTE  The findings are nonspecific and suggestive of post inflammatory  changes  A repeat biopsy on an active lesion may be more informative and is  advised  if clinically appropriate   B  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST  PUNCH     Sparse perivascular chronic inflammation with dermal mucin deposition   NOTE  The changes are nonspecific but raise the possibility of connective  tissue disease  including tumid lupus erythematosus  reticular erythematous  mucinosis  and delayed type hypersensitivity reactions  Serologic testing to  exclude Lyme disease is advised  if clinically appropriate  Clinical  correlation is needed   C  SKIN  LEFT SHOULDER  PUNCH   This specimen shows similar features to those in specimen  B   In addition   however  at the base of the biopsy is a nodular lymphocytic aggregate that is  of uncertain biological significance  This finding raises the possibility  deeper more significant pathology  possibly lupus profundus but these biopsies  are too superficial for definitive evaluation  A deeper biopsy to allow for  more definitive diagnosis is advised if clinically significant  A silver stain  is negative for spirochetes   Case reviewed at Dermatopathology Division Staff Conference   Case discussed with Dr  Haynes   CLINICAL DATA   History  50 year old F with a 31 year history of DLE on Plaquenil and  quinacrine  who presents with alopecia and erythematous patches on L shoulder  and R breast   Operation  A  4 mm Punch  B  3 mm Punch  C  3 mm Punch   Operative Findings   A  Patch of alopecia  non erythematous  non scarring L scalp   B  R breast erythematous patch   C  L shoulder erythematous patch   Clinical Diagnosis  A  Alopecia areata vs  DLE  B C  DLE   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Skin  L scalp   B 2  Skin  R breast   C 3  Skin  L shoulder   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received in formalin  in three parts  each labeled with the  patient s name and unit number   Part A  labeled   1  Left scalp   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  depth   tan brown hair bearing circular skin  inked and embedded in toto   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 frag  ESS   Part B  labeled   2  Right breast   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  depth   light tan circular skin  inked and embedded in toto   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 frag  ESS   Part C  labeled   3  Left shoulder   consists of a 0 3cm diameter x 0 4cm  depth light tan circular skin  inked and embedded in toto   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 frag  ESS   CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_CASE_ID   By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Scott R Granter M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
