or resection margin is re inked in yellow  and the following sections are taken  The nodule is submitted entirely in cassette A through J  cassettes A and B represent the lateral aspect of the nodule  3 5cm from the lateral resection margin   and cassettes I and J represents the medial aspect of the nodule  3 7cm from the medial resection margin   Sections through the lateral inferior area of fibrosis are submitted in cassettes K through M  Sections through grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma taken 1 7cm from the medial resection margin are submitted in cassette N and O  Skin and subcutaneous tissue overlying the closest  3 2cm   portion of the nodule is submitted as cassette P  Breast tissue at the lateral resection margin is submitted as Q  Breast tissue at the medial resection margin is submitted as R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
