e lateral tissue of the breast after an  extensive gross and microscopic examination of this tissue   This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a NX MX   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 54 year old female with ADH and DCIS   I m worried about an invasive  component at  6 00 just below areola  Took low axillary nodes  3 5 or so   probable    Operation  Left simple mastectomy with tissue expander  Clinical Diagnosis  DCIS left breast  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Left breast   stitch axilla  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by WOLGAMOT GREGORY M  M D  PH D   The specimen is received fresh in one part  labeled with the patient s name   unit number and   1  left breast   stitch axilla   and consists of a simple  mastectomy specimen  127g  15 x 10 x 2 5cm overall   The specimen contains a  skin ellipse  7 5 x 2 5cm   with a somewhat indistinct areola  2 5cm diameter   and a nipple  1 4cm diameter   No cutaneous scars are evident  The deep  fascial plane  which is glistening smooth and slides easily over the specimen   is inked in black   The specimen is radiographed  and the radiograph reveals multiple small  calcifications in the upper outer quadrant  a large calcification medial to  the nipple  and a density inferior to the nipple   The breast is composed of approximately 70  white fibrous tissue and 30   adipose tissue  Approximately 2cm inferior to the nipple is a firm white mass   1 5cm   with circumscribed borders  The mass has a central cavitation  0 4cm  diameter  consistent with a prior biopsy site  A hemorrhage tract extends from  this region medially  associated with fat necrosis  The firm mass is  approximately 0 7cm from the deep margin  No other masses are identified in  the specimen  The tissue in the lateral portion is fixed in Bouin s and  thinly sectioned  No definite lymph nodes are identified  The tissue is  extensively sampled   Micro REMOVED_DATE  mass at 6 o clock  1 frag each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue adjacent to mass  1 frag each  RSS