al to lateral to reveal a diffusely  intermixed white fibrous tissue  20 30  of specimen  with yellow adipose  tissue  No discrete masses or lesions are present  There is one focus of  hemorrhage  0 7cm in greatest dimension   possibly corresponding to the prior  biopsy site  One hundred per cent  100   of the fibrous tissue is submitted   Micro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue from medial to lateral  excluding medial  and lateral tips  1 frag each  ESS  Micro 12   17  medial perpendicular tip  3 frags cass  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular tip  12 frags  ESS  Part two  labeled   2  posterior shave margin  right breast with stitch  margins  short stitch   superior  long stitch   lateral   consists of one  fragment of fibroadipose tissue  3 4cm medial to lateral  2cm superior to  inferior and 1 0cm posterior to anterior   The specimen comes with the  posterior surface inked black by the surgeon and a long suture marking the  lateral side  The remaining sides are inked by the pathologist per pathology  protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue   superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  The short stitch  designating the superior surface arises at the junction between the superior  and anterior surfaces  Per conversation with the surgeon in the prosecting  room  the only margin of interest is the posterior margin  The specimen was  serially sectioned to reveal primarily fibroadipose tissue   10  fibrous  tissue  with no lesions present  One hundred per cent  100   of the fibrous  tissue is submitted   Micro REMOVED_DATE  posterior shave margin  1 frag each  RSS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  lateral posterior shave margin  7 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  posterior shave margin from lateral to medial  1 frag each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  medial posterior shave margin  4 frags each  ESS  sak  Reports to  CHRISTIAN  ROGER  L  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN