Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Kristina Braaten  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  CLINICAL DATA  ADH on core biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  FOCUS OF SEVERE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  GREATER THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM ALL MARGINS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   PRESENT THROUGHOUT THE TISSUE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  CALCIFICATIONS INVOLVING FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND LOBULES INVOLVED BY LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  Note  Results of immunohistochemical stains for E cadherin support the presence of both ductal hyperplasia and lobular neoplasia  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue with an inserted wire  A short stitch denotes the anterior margin  a long stitch the lateral margin and a bow tie the cephalad position  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink  the posterior margin with black ink  the superior margin with green ink and the inferior margin with yellow ink  The specimen is serially sectioned from the lateral to the medial aspect to reveal a 1 1cm in diameter biopsy cavity at the medial end of the specimen  0 4cm from the medial margin  This cavity corresponds to the lesion seen on the specimen radiograph which is at the hooked end of the wire  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  tan lesion with irregular borders which extends from the lateral side of the aforementioned biopsy cavity and to 1 5cm of the lateral margin  There is a clip identified in the lesion in the mid portion of the specimen  The lesion is located 0 4cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the posterior margin  0 9cm from the superior margin  1 5cm from the inferior margin and greater than 2 0cm from the medial margin  Approximately 60  of the remainder of the specimen consists of soft  white fibrous tissue with the remaining tissue being soft  lobulated  yellow adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   from the lateral to the medial end with the lesion in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The medial margin is submitted en face in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from the medial to the lateral aspect  Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , no_TubularCancer.
 REMOVED_CASE_ID  JAYAWARDENE MAKEVITAGE 48 F  REG REF 10 24    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC NEWTON CHEH EMILY M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  10 24 08  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  Indeterminate right breast calcifications  rule out ductal carcinoma in situ Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereo biopsies  right breast  and contains an aqua cassette which is designated on the specimen requisition form to contain the specimen microcalcifications  Within this aqua cassette is a 0 6cm  long  0 3cm  in diameter yellowish red  firm  glistening needle biopsy  The specimen is marked with green ink  Also present free floating within the specimen container is a 2 x 2 x 0 3cm  aggregate of yellowish red soft needle biopsies admixed with blood clot measuring 0 3cm  in diameter  The specimens are marked with green ink  Section code  1   tissue in aqua cassette with specimen microcalcifications   1X all  2   free floating tissue   1 agg  all  Total fixation time is 12 hours  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD DIAGNOSIS  Right breast  needle core biopsies  Pools of mucin with microcalcifications and adjacent detached strips of epithelium  see note   Microcalcifications also identified in adipose tissue  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  The specimen consists of mostly adipose tissue with scant benign breast ducts and lobules  Both blocks of tissue show pools of mucin  Microcalcifications are identified within the mucin and within the adipose tissue  Adjacent to the mucin and focally within the mucin are strips of detached  fairly benign appearing epithelium  Both blocks of tissue have been completely leveled through  The pools of mucin are worrisome for mucinous carcinoma  however  a diagnosis of mucinous carcinoma cannot be made on this material given the lack of atypical epithelial cells within the mucin  Radiographic pathologic correlation is recommended and repeat biopsies may be indicated  especially if a mass lesion is identified  Final Diagnosis by  Nicole A  Mihok  M D  DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT   Continued  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD MIHN Notes  REMOVED_DATE  In addition to the cosigner Dr  Abbott  Dr  Mattia has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis  NAM Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Epithelium  NOS  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Right breast  N Needle  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Right breast  N Mucin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Adipose tissue BREANBX    BREANBX BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Separation  NOS Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCOPIES TO  CAHILL TERESA M D  NWH RADIOLOGY DEPT  NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 243  REMOVED_CASE_ID  NEWTON CHEH EMILY M D   REMOVED_CASE_ID  WASHINGTON ST  NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 965  REMOVED_CASE_ID MARKERS  Breast Disease Related Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORDPROCEDURES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   10 28 08  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJTISSUES  Breast  needle biopsy   right Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORDFinal  ABBOTT TODD MD   REMOVED_DATE  10 28 08  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD ABBT MIHOK NICOLE MD        REMOVED_DATE  10 28 08  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD MIHN                                     