Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D   LEFT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A LOBULATED MASS AND A CLIP MARKING A  PRIOR CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY   SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA involving a sclerosing papilloma   block 10  levels examined   see note   An immunohistochemical study for  p63 reveals basally located myoepithelial cells throughout the lesion  as  well as scattered cells within the areas of hyperplasia  The entire  sclerosing papilloma measures 0 8cm in size   The closest margin is lateral which is   0 1cm from the sclerosing  papilloma   The prior core needle biopsy site is present associated with the  sclerosing papilloma   Note  This lesion is evaluated in conjunction with the prior core needle  biopsy  BWH consultation  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and both show similar features   The hyperplasia is difficult to evaluate due to the involvement of the  papilloma  Areas of the hyperplasia demonstrate regular cribriform  spaces  Some of the spaces are filled with mucin or basement membrane  material  suggestive of mucinous and collagenous spherulosis  This is  supported by the p63 study which suggests that the epithelial  proliferation is made up of both luminal and myoepithelial cells   However  other spaces appear empty  more typical of DCIS   The differential diagnosis includes a low grade DCIS versus ADH involving  a papilloma  The latter diagnosis is favored due to the lack of  definitive areas of DCIS outside the area of this focal lesion  However   the lesion is very close to the margin  Re excision may be helpful to  exclude an adjacent area of DCIS   Dr  James Connolly reviewed selected slides and concurs with the  interpretation of this lesion as severely atypical ductal hyperplasia   CLINICAL DATA   History  Status post core biopsy REMOVED_DATE    DCIS   Operation  Left wire localized partial mastectomy   TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Left wire localized partial mastectomy   Radiology report   Mass and clip are in specimen  Dr  S  Durfee  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by O CONNELL FIONNUALA MB BCH BAO  The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number   and   1  left wire localized partial mastectomy   and consists of a single  fragment of pink tan fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The specimen has  a localization wire protruding from it  The specimen is inked per pathology  protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior   blue   superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange  The  interior of the specimen is mostly fat  with scant fibrous tissue  A core  needle biopsy site spans the length of the specimen from the anterior to the  posterior aspect  No obvious mass is noted adjacent to the core biopsy site or  within any other area of the specimen  The specimen is serially sectioned and  entirely submitted  The specimen is submitted with an accompanying specimen  radiograph  which demonstrates the presence of a localizing wire  mass and a  clip   Micro REMOVED_DATE  anterior  ESS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  posterior  ESS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of the specimen  anterior to posterior  ESS   fsd  Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY  M PH  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE   report_end  , no_TubularCancer.
